      "Language": "fre",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "We report a case of complete rupture of the radial collateral ligament of the fifth metacarpophalangeal joint. At surgical exploration, a Stener like lesion was identified in which the ruptured and of the ligament was trapped by the proximal portion of the extensor hood and sagittal band; thus reattachment to its original site (the base of proximal phalanx) was performed. Postoperative care consisted of protected active motion exercises which were begun immediately. An early functional recovery was obtained with full range of motion, normal joint stability and complete pain relief. The purpose of this study was to present an uncommon injury and to analyse the literature."},
